---
title: Passeridae
---
# Passeridae

Passeridae is the Old World sparrow family, small, thick-billed seed-eaters
closely associated with human settlement. The bill is deep and conical, suited
to cracking hard seed, and the plumage is a subdued brown and grey in which the
male is distinguished by a dark bib. They build a domed nest of grass wedged
into a hole in a wall, and they are gregarious throughout the year, feeding in
flocks and roosting communally in dense cover. See [[house-sparrow]].
